@startuml system-context
!include _theme.iuml
left to right direction

actor "Repository operator" as Operator
actor "CI/CD workflow" as Automation
actor "TypeScript application" as Application

rectangle "Octoform system boundary" as Octoform {
  rectangle "Command-line interface\nCommands, options, confirmation, reports" as CLI
  rectangle "Public ESM API\nTyped configuration, planning and apply exports" as API
  rectangle "Governance engine\nResolve policy, observe state, plan and apply" as Engine
}

cloud "GitHub REST API\nOwner identity, repositories, organization metadata,\nsettings and governed resources" as GitHub

Operator --> CLI : audit, classify, plan, apply
Automation --> CLI : scheduled audit, PR plan, protected apply
Application --> API : typed function calls
CLI --> Engine : validated command intent
API --> Engine : typed service invocation
Engine --> GitHub : authenticated reads and permitted writes
GitHub --> Engine : current state, permissions and capability evidence
Engine --> CLI : findings, plan, outcomes and exit status
Engine --> API : typed values, changes and errors

note bottom of Octoform
  One resolved configuration targets one owner in 0.3.
  The released integration uses GitHub REST, not GraphQL.
end note
@enduml
